"Between the separate bones lie 23 soft cushions called discs. A disc has a tough ring on the outside and a soft gel in the middle, a little like a jelly doughnut. The discs let your spine bend, and they soak up the bumps when you run and jump. Do you remember that you are a little taller in the morning than at night? During the day your discs are squeezed, and at night, when you lie down, they fill up again.": "eab9d632d60a",
"Can you help me carry these bags?": "cff0eb31c764",
"Draw a straight line with a ruler.": "8343b8873e00",
"Look at a spine from the side, and you will see that it is not straight. It curves in at the neck, out at the upper back, and in again at the lower back. A newborn baby has only one long curve. The neck curve forms when the baby learns to hold up its head, and the lower curve forms when the child learns to walk. These curves make the spine stronger and springier, like the bends in a spring.": "20186f5dde69",
